Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:41:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: ilp32: vDSO: data page is two pages below the code

Since the time namespace support the vvar area has two pages (vDSO data, then
the time namespace page), and the vDSO code finds its data at
". - __VVAR_PAGES * PAGE_SIZE", as the LP64 and AArch32 vDSOs do. The ILP32
linker script still had the older "_vdso_data = . - PAGE_SIZE" in front of
the new definition, and the first PROVIDE wins: _vdso_data was 0xfffff000
instead of 0xffffe000, so every vDSO call read the time namespace page and,
without a time namespace, got SIGBUS (e.g. clock_gettime() in glibc).

Remove the old line. Found in QEMU; the same line is in openEuler
OLK-5.10 and OLK-6.6.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5481775506b69b1dab1ed519fcec935b12ab3ead)
(cherry picked from commit 52fad911f2dd7cbccd492a8792406d18b9370e61)
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/vdso-ilp32/vdso-ilp32.lds.S | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/vdso-ilp32/vdso-ilp32.lds.S
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/vdso-ilp32/vdso-ilp32.lds.S
@@ -14,7 +14,6 @@
 
 SECTIONS
 {
-	PROVIDE(_vdso_data = . - PAGE_SIZE);
 	PROVIDE(_vdso_data = . - __VVAR_PAGES * PAGE_SIZE);
 #ifdef CONFIG_TIME_NS
 	PROVIDE(_timens_data = _vdso_data + PAGE_SIZE);
